<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:00.550
<b>Cloudy, Then Rainy?</b>

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:03.560
Um...

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.470
So, uh... Sagara-senpai
and Sawa-senpai went home.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.980
They said, "Good luck, Daigo-kyun."

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.210
They went home?

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:14.820
How come?!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.280
Who knows.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.940
I'm goin' after 'em.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.050
Anita.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:21.820
It's fine.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.700
Let's just concentrate on the game.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.090
<i>Eihou's ace, Jitou.</i>

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.800
<i>140 kmph is a bit of an exaggeration,</i>

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.910
<i>but his fastballs are consistently
over the 130 kmph mark.</i>

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.460
<i>He's several notches faster than Yokouchi 
and Urabe, and we did fastball drills for them.</i>

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.240
Guess there's a reason these guys
are the team to beat in our district.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.780
Yeah, their offense packs a punch, too.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.200
<i>They get hits all the way down the order.</i>

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:22.430
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:22.430
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:22.430
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:22.430
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.880
<i>I wanted to check out their batters some more,
but what I saw depressed me too much.</i>

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.200
Bow!

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.190
Thank you!

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.700
They're so strong.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.230
We're going to get destroyed.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.710
No wonder Tao and Yayoi just left like that.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.440
Beating them is impossible.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.150
Looks 'bout right.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.880
S'obvious we were gonna run into this
kinda hurdle on our way to Regionals.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.880
Beatin' them'll be worth it.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:43.990
Gonna be fun.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.120
I'm looking forward to seeing
how far my pitching gets us.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.040
You guys are right.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.670
Looks like we've got no choice but to
put Nishina on the mound in the final.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.580
Problem is, who will we get to
pitch in our semifinal game?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:14.480
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:14.480
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:14.480
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:14.480
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.680
I think you'd do fine against
Yanagawa Middle, Mutsuko,

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.430
but it'd be your third game in three days.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:12.020
Pitching a complete game when
you're already exhausted is a tough ask,

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.830
and I don't want you to overdo it.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.300
So what's the plan?

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:18.900
Chisato.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.080
You pitched for Yokohama Little, right?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.450
I want you and Mutsuko to get us through
tomorrow's game with Yanagawa.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.220
Are you sure I'm up for it?

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.460
Yes. I'm counting on you.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.040
All right.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.240
Great.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.000
How about we go back to school now
and you can show me your pitching?

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.460
Right now?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.300
Hey, Shigeno.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.650
We just finished a game.
Fujii's probably tired.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.180
You shouldn't go overboard.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.470
It's true we don't need to push
ourselves hard for the next game,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.140
but we've got a chance of facing Eihou,
so I want to give it all we've got.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.480
Is it too much?

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.100
No, I'll go.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.860
I-I'm coming too!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.070
Yeah, okay. It might be
better if you're there.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.280
I bet you want to check out 
my hyper-speed pitches, too.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.760
Yup.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.780
As you are now, you don't 
stand a chance against Eihou.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.040
Mifune Baseball Park

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.040
All right, anyone not heading back
to school is done for the day.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.460
Good job, everyone!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.110
Good job!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.750
Get some rest, guys.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.710
Okay.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.680
Captain!

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.200
I oughta be the one goin' back 
to school an' catchin' their pitches.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.180
I'm sorry.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.320
Don't sweat it.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.860
Right now, getting over your
injury is your top priority.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.390
Hurry up and get it checked out.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.810
Then, I'll leave it to ya, Captain.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:41.120
Hey! You're getting left behind!

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.480
Coming!

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.400
Later, Anita.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.790
Ouch...

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.380
<i>I'm injured, so I can't go practice 
with 'em, even though I wanna.</i>

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.230
<i>But there ain't anythin' wrong
with Sagara-senpai or Sawa-senpai,</i>

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.840
<i>so why'd they go home instead
of watchin' Eihou's game with us?</i>

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>Team</b>

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>Yoshisawa Little</b>

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>Yokohama Little</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.340
<b>Team</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.340
<b>Yoshisawa Little</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.340
<b>Yokohama Little</b>

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:14.680
Yes!

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:15.820
We've got someone on first!

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.600
This is still anyone's game.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.490
A-All right!

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.530
Dang, looks like you stole my spotlight.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.280
Couldn't have done it without your setup.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.750
<i>I've admired those two
ever since I was in Little.</i>

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.500
<i>Both of 'em were already doin' amazin' things
even before I started wearin' the mask.</i>

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.350
<i>Please lemme keep admirin' you forever...</i>

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:55.340
D'you think that was a bit mean,
running out on Daigo?

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.600
Not even a little.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:01.170
His relentless can-do attitude
is honestly exhausting at times.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.060
There's no way we can beat Eihou, anyway.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.650
What if they all went back to school 
to practice after the Eihou game?

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:09.440
Nah, surely not.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.610
Oh, wait, that actually does sound
like something Daigo would suggest.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.770
Jeez, it's not like a few random practice
sessions are the answer to everything.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.110
Especially for you, Yayoi—

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.180
Well, I'm not letting baseball eat into
my downtime after a game on a weekend.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.140
Right?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:34.470
I mean, I like baseball. I really do.
But don't you wonder sometimes?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.920
If this is all our middle 
school years are about?

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:38.680
Meaning?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.410
This is our youth, you know? Our youth!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:44.180
At this rate, it'll be three years later,
and all we'll have done

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.940
is sweat our asses off on the field,
chasing a white ball around!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.850
I think getting sweaty on a baseball field
 and chasing a white ball around

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:54.410
is exactly what adults call "youth."

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.400
What?

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.870
But the "youth" you're talking about
is something like that, right?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:00.960
Say "Ah."

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:01.830
Ah.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:07.290
I can't go to high school and admit
to people I've never had a boyfriend!

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.730
I get where you're coming from.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:13.760
Wouldn't it be nice to be like Mutsuko
and have a crush on someone on our team?

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.220
Right... Wait, what did you just say?

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.350
Don't tell me you haven't noticed.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.220
Who is it?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:21.820
Daigo?

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:22.310
Nishina?

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:25.510
Hey now, what happened to Tanba-san?

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:27.020
No way it's him.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.120
Okay!

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:30.940
Let's go.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.400
Okay.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.830
That was nice!

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:46.160
Huh. Those are pretty fast.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:49.120
Not nearly as fast as mine, of course.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.570
But probably faster than—

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:51.050
Hm?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.970
Oh, nothing.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.100
Looking good!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.890
By the way, can you throw any breaking balls?

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:06.100
I'm not sure, but I'll give it a try.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.240
That's a bit mean of Daigo.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:13.520
Chisato's a first-year. She can't 
just casually throw breaking balls.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.070
After all, grade schoolers
are banned from using them.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:19.490
Nice ball!

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:21.950
A slider?

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.900
Breaking balls are only
banned in rubber-ball.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.960
But she played Little League.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.950
I liked that slider!

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.920
Your control was good, too.
We can really use these!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.100
Oh, really?

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.070
I'm so happy!

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.140
Thank you!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.830
I think Fujii just secured
the starting pitcher spot.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.410
What? I was just saying.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:45.330
Good work today.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.470
Hey, Daigo! I'm pretty tired, so I'm heading home.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.570
Uh, okay. Good job today.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.370
Good luck, Chisato.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.350
I'll try!

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.660
Pitcher?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:10.890
Yeah. We don't have a pitcher right now, you see.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:16.670
Well, yeah, but I'm sure one of
the new sign-ups in spring will want to pitch.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:19.290
Spring's way too late.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.860
We won't know if we can
throw them straight into a game,

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:26.350
so we need to train up at least 
one pitcher from our current roster.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.810
See? Good pitchers signed up after all.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:46.620
Ack, I'm soaked through.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.500
I didn't know it was gonna rain today.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.540
Izumi-senpai?

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:54.730
Hi!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.010
Well, isn't this a crazy coincidence!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.540
Right?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.620
Are you coming back from a game?

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.560
Your second game was today, wasn't it?

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:11.440
Yes.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.240
So how'd it go?

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.500
We won.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.970
It was really close, but still...

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.440
Wow, that's awesome!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.000
So is it the semi-finals tomorrow?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.750
Yeah, looks like.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:25.470
The fact you made it this far
with your useless captain

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.410
means the ace must be rock solid.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:28.840
Oh, no...

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.660
Besides, it's all thanks to you.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.500
You taught me how to throw breaking balls.

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:37.960
You were a quick learner,
so teaching you was fun for me too.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.150
Put your middle finger on the stitching.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:41.930
Yeah, like that.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:45.510
Don't twist. Slice it like... this.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.560
Don't twist, slice.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:51.860
Since then, I've also learned 
how to do pickoff attempts.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:56.430
There are so many things a pitcher
needs to learn. It's a bit overwhelming.

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:58.720
But still fun, right?

00:11:58.720 --> 00:11:59.900
Yes!

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:08.830
Which is why I'd really like
to be pitching all the time.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:13.240
Today, I ran out of steam
in the middle of the game,

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.530
and tomorrow, another girl
might be the starting pitcher.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.820
Mutsuko-chan, tomorrow would
be your third day in a row, right?

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:25.070
Then, it's totally normal.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.970
I suppose.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:38.770
I bet you feel a strong sense 
of responsibility for the team.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:39.840
Huh?

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.310
You're a bit like Daigo in that way.

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.700
Heh, I guess that's a bit of an insult,
comparing you to him.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.800
I thought this was gonna be a shower,
but doesn't look like it's stopping.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.270
Here you go.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.650
You can use this umbrella, if you like.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.860
I'll just sprint home.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.020
Oh, I couldn't!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.020
You should take it!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.980
I'll be fine. I'll run home.

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:21.690
Daigo would be super mad if I let his ace 
catch a cold the day before the semi-finals.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:24.860
Take it.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.140
See ya.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.610
Good luck tomorrow.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.010
The rain's getting even worse.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.320
No signs of it letting up.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.850
Let's call it a day.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.100
Huh? Seriously?

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.040
Okay.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.580
I'm off, then.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:58.540
H-Hey! I haven't thrown a single pitch yet!

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.870
That's too bad.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.940
Let's get going before we catch a chill.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:04.940
What the hell?!

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:08.240
This rain won't dampen my pitching spirit!

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.530
Okay, you win this round, rain.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:18.290
<i>Man, the weather forecast was way off.</i>

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.540
Nishina?

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:24.590
You on your way home?

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:25.370
Yeah.

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.170
You guys just finished practice, too?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.340
Yeah, more or less.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.720
So are you still on that all-girls' team?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.560
Yeah, more or less.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.020
You ain't got it easy, huh?

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.470
What about you?

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:39.440
How are you doing in Senior League?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.230
You all starters yet?

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.370
Are you really in any position
to worry about us?

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:45.590
I heard, y'know.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:50.200
I know they still haven't let you pitch
in your girls' rubber-ball team.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.450
C'mon, dude, your info's outta date.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.660
They want me to be the 
starting pitcher in the final.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.410
Against Eihou, no less.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:02.830
Looks like those fools finally 
realized how good I really am.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.130
This is the beginning of my saga!

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.590
Huh?

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.090
Looks like you're having a good time.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.890
You've really meshed with that team, huh.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:17.350
Totally the opposite.
They're meshing with me!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:21.310
<b>Hayashida Chiropractor</b>

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:21.310
<b>Hayashida Chiropractor</b>

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:18.940
Take care.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.810
Thank you.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.520
<i>One week for it to fully heal.</i>

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.560
<i>I'm happy as heck it's only a light sprain.</i>

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:34.090
<i>The doc told me I oughtn't play tomorrow,
but that ain't a luxury I can afford.</i>

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.210
Seriously? It's rainin'?!

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.910
Aw man, this sucks. I ain't got an umbrella.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:45.380
No, wait, this is great!

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:48.510
If the game gets postponed 
to next week 'cause of the rain,

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.590
my wrist'll be all healed up by then!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.220
Rain harder!

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.050
Postpone the game!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:58.520
Wow, I never knew Mutsuko
had a thing for Daigo.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.390
Seriously, are you blind?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.710
It's pretty obvious just by looking at them.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.140
Oh. It's raining.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:09.440
Ah. Wonder if they'll
postpone tomorrow's game.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:14.040
Not that it matters when we play Eihou.
The result will be the same.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.070
Hey, Yayoi, do you have an umbrella?

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.080
Just a folding one.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.590
That's some top-tier girl skills!

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.580
Can we share it to the station?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.090
Batting Center
<b>Mifune Dome</b>

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.090
Batting Center
<b>Mifune Dome</b>

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.970
This time!

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.930
<i>I can't keep holding the team back!</i>

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:46.940
This time!

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.070
Batting Center
<b>Mifune Dome</b>

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.070
Batting Center
<b>Mifune Dome</b>

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.070
This time!

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.870
First!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.540
<i>I'm the only third-year on the team.</i>

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:16.800
<i>I can't let the younger guys see this 
pathetic version of me anymore.</i>

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.470
I'm home!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.090
Welcome back.

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.930
So how'd it go, Chisato?

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.650
Oh, we won.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.700
And our semi-final opponent looks beatable,

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.300
so we'll probably make the final.

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:37.070
And tomorrow, I'm going to pitch as well.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.660
That's fantastic!

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.080
I'll definitely be there to cheer you on.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.420
But don't you have a Dolphins game tomorrow?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.700
Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.760
I should be able to make it to the final, though.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.380
Wait for me on the mound, Chisato.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.840
I think they're getting someone 
else to pitch in the final.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.520
That's fine, too!

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.460
All right! Let's go winjoy some pork
cutlet rice bowl to bring you luck!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.850
I just finished making dinner.
I fried up some ginger pork.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.380
What did you say you
were going to go eat?

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.880
I-It was a joke!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:18.240
You make the best food, Miho.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.410
Hang in there, Dad.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.000
So I heard you won again.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.280
You're on a roll.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.680
Maybe I'll come watch your game tomorrow.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.380
You don't have to.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.890
This next game is going to be 
more of a test run, anyway.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:50.800
I'll give you credit for making
it this far with that team.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.400
But are you on top of it?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.460
On top of what?

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.980
The mental side.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:57.170
Especially with your ace.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:19:00.950
You're the captain, so it's your job
to keep on top of these things.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.770
Our ace?

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.410
Something up with Mutsuko?

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:09.120
You really don't have the slightest clue?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.510
Pitching two games in a row
has really tired her out,

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.310
so I decided to use two
pitchers in tomorrow's game.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.800
But that's for her sake too.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:22.550
Even if it's for her, you have to
consider how delicate a girl's heart is!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.060
It might not be in Mutsuko-chan's 
interest to say too much.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:32.260
Daigo is just as dense as his father.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.540
You're right.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.230
It was foolish of me to try.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:37.230
Huh?

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:43.070
<i>And now, the weather for the 
Kantou Koushinetsu area.</i>

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:48.160
<i>Intermittent showers will continue 
through the night and into the early hours.</i>

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:53.370
<i>But the rain will clear up by morning,
and we should see some sun in the afternoon.</i>

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:57.030
<i>The field will be in bad shape.
I wonder if they'll cancel the game.</i>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:02.940
<i>Considering Anita's injury and Mutsuko's 
fatigue, that might work out better for us.</i>

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.490
Izumi, can you get that?

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:08.990
Sure.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:14.270
Oh, actually, I think I need
the toilet, like right now.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.870
Daigo, can you get it?

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.060
What?

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:20.610
Hello?

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.200
Mutsuko?

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:25.650
What are you doing here this late?

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.900
I ran into Izumi-senpai earlier,

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.370
and she lent me this.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:33.010
I wanted to return it as soon as possible.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.830
You could've just given it to me tomorrow.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.540
Well, I guess, but...

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.010
I'm glad I got a chance to see you, though.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:49.430
You looked so tired earlier.
I'm relieved you're looking better.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.960
<i>Oh, that's what he meant.</i>

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:55.230
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.660
Yeah. Later.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.460
What is wrong with you?!

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:05.800
Walk her home this instant!

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.240
That's right, Daigo!

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:13.910
I kinda feel bad.

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:16.040
Now you're walking me home.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.090
Oh, no, it's not a problem.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:23.690
You know...

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:23.690
You know...

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:28.430
Oh, sorry. Go ahead.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:32.890
It wasn't important.
What were you going to say?

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:37.350
No, I was just thinking...

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.820
I hope it doesn't stop raining.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:48.620
Yeah.

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:04.420
This is bad. The ground's so soggy,
it's just one error after the other!

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:06.690
This game's gonna be tough, Sekitori-senpai.

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:08.490
It's "Kandori," not "Sekitori." I'm not a sumo.

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:11.230
Anyway, why are all
the girls getting so tense?

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:12.590
What's going on?

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.550
Girls have a lot to worry about, okay?

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:17.030
Like what? How to season your sumo stew?

00:24:17.030 --> 00:24:18.790
That'll go down sumooth!
Wait, that's not a Sekitori's job!

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:20.020
Aren't you a Kandori?!

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Semi-Finals Time!</b>

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:22.600
Next time: "Semi-Finals Time!"

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:25.020
Run to the stage of your dreams!
